WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:01.720
Not getting enough sleep

00:00:01.720 --> 00:00:03.860
won't just make you cranky.

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:05.410
It could kill you.

00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:08.240
The United Nations even
considers sleep deprivation

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:10.160
a form of torture.

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:13.820
And the longer it lasts,
the worse it'll get.

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:16.260
Losing sleep affects people differently,

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:19.840
but generally the effects
increase as the hours do.

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:22.150
Just 48 hours without sleep is considered

00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:24.370
extreme sleep deprivation,

00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:27.200
but you'll probably get weird before then.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:29.033
After 18 hours with no sleep,

00:00:29.033 --> 00:00:30.950
you might feel a little drunk.

00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:32.700
Staying awake that long is equivalent

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:36.960
to having a blood
alcohol content of 0.05%,

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:39.280
which is what you get
with three or four drinks

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:40.982
in the span of two hours.

00:00:40.982 --> 00:00:42.598
24 sleepless hours,

00:00:42.598 --> 00:00:46.464
that BAC comparison jumps to 0.1%,

00:00:46.464 --> 00:00:49.510
higher than the legal
driving limit in every state.

00:00:49.510 --> 00:00:53.170
You might feel foggy, less
alert, or uncoordinated,

00:00:53.170 --> 00:00:55.470
almost like you're wearing
sleepy beer goggles,

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:57.820
including double or blurry vision.

00:00:57.820 --> 00:01:00.420
That's because sleep
deprivation slows down

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:03.280
our brain cells' ability
to talk to each other.

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:05.600
So if you actually are drinking alcohol,

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:08.100
drowsiness can increase its effects.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:09.875
And while caffeine could make you feel

00:01:09.875 --> 00:01:11.716
more alert for several hours,

00:01:11.716 --> 00:01:14.310
it'll only work up to a certain point.

00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:15.451
By a day and a half,

00:01:15.451 --> 00:01:17.759
this could all get worse and then some.

00:01:17.759 --> 00:01:19.970
Your chances of getting
sick are higher than usual

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:22.720
because your body can't
fight like it normally can,

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:26.440
and around this time, your
brain and body get so tired

00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:28.910
that you start experiencing microsleeps,

00:01:28.910 --> 00:01:31.860
tiny periods of sleep,
maybe around 30 seconds,

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:33.580
that you might not even notice.

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:36.210
Definitely annoying and even dangerous

00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:38.540
if you're doing something
like driving a car.

00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:41.270
And then there's the
potential for hallucinations.

00:01:41.270 --> 00:01:43.460
Visual distortions are most common.

00:01:43.460 --> 00:01:45.910
Your water bottle grows to twice its size

00:01:45.910 --> 00:01:47.690
or moves around the room.

00:01:47.690 --> 00:01:49.820
But you could also experience sensational

00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:51.800
or auditory hallucinations,

00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:53.920
things like feeling
someone who's not there

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:56.877
tap you on the shoulder or
hearing your name being called.

00:01:56.877 --> 00:01:57.860
[ghostly voice whispering inaudibly]

00:01:57.860 --> 00:02:01.110
Once you hit 48 hours,
it's literal torture,

00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:03.340
which is why
extreme-sleep-deprivation studies

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:06.600
are now prohibited by
law in most countries.

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:08.360
Two days without sleep can cause you

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:11.035
to start losing your grip on reality.

00:02:11.035 --> 00:02:12.520
Hallucinations worsen,

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:15.250
and you might even
undergo depersonalization.

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:18.150
That's the feeling that
reality is slipping away,

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:22.060
which may or may not include
an out-of-body experience.

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:25.990
Tack on extreme anxiety,
irritability, stress, and fatigue,

00:02:25.990 --> 00:02:27.970
and it's no wonder the UN doesn't allow

00:02:27.970 --> 00:02:29.740
this kind of deprivation.

00:02:29.740 --> 00:02:32.410
After 72 hours, you're
not gonna be able to think

00:02:32.410 --> 00:02:34.740
about anything but hitting the hay.

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:36.520
Forget about doing simple tasks.

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:39.080
Things like getting
dressed or finding a snack

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:42.200
could feel overwhelming,
partially from fatigue

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:45.140
and partially because your
ability to regulate emotions

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:47.050
is basically out the window.

00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:49.600
Your hallucinations
could get more complex,

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:53.210
creating fully formed images
like a person, or a bear,

00:02:53.210 --> 00:02:55.760
or maybe a car you shouldn't drive.

00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:58.460
And in at least four
historical sleep studies,

00:02:58.460 --> 00:03:01.390
participants reported
shared hallucinations,

00:03:01.390 --> 00:03:03.840
namely something called
the hat phenomenon,

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:06.590
which is basically a feeling
of pressure around your head

00:03:06.590 --> 00:03:08.670
as if you're wearing a hat.

00:03:08.670 --> 00:03:11.020
All of this opens the door for paranoia,

00:03:11.020 --> 00:03:13.300
depression, and delusions.

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:17.120
Which brings us to 96 hours
or more with no sleep.

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:19.520
Say bye-bye to reality, folks.

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:22.358
More and worse hallucinations and paranoia

00:03:22.358 --> 00:03:25.270
could lead to sleep-deprivation psychosis,

00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:27.630
a total snap from the real world.

00:03:27.630 --> 00:03:30.072
Historically, women
accused of being witches

00:03:30.072 --> 00:03:33.500
were kept awake long enough
to trigger this psychosis.

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:36.770
Judges considered their visions
and ramblings confessions,

00:03:36.770 --> 00:03:39.270
leading to the women's convictions.

00:03:39.270 --> 00:03:42.900
Now, the fifth day is sometimes
called the turning point.

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:44.990
This is the danger zone.

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:47.530
Your mental health takes a sharp decline,

00:03:47.530 --> 00:03:50.420
cementing your delusions
as your new reality.

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:52.900
Eventually, your brain will
stop functioning properly

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:55.250
in a way that could lead to organ failure

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:58.180
and, in rare cases, death.

00:03:58.180 --> 00:04:00.440
Luckily, recovering from sleep deprivation

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:03.230
can be as simple as catching up on sleep,

00:04:03.230 --> 00:04:05.160
but if you're sleep deprived regularly,

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:06.830
you're looking at long-term effects

00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:08.988
like weight gain, acne, headaches,

00:04:08.988 --> 00:04:11.610
and high blood pressure,
among other things.

00:04:11.610 --> 00:04:14.090
And it can take weeks
to get back on track.

00:04:14.090 --> 00:04:15.120
According to one study,

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:17.177
you need four days to recover

00:04:17.177 --> 00:04:20.510
from losing a single hour of sleep.

00:04:20.510 --> 00:04:23.540
Try getting to bed early
instead of sleeping in late,

00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:27.330
or, better yet, avoid the
recovery period entirely

00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:30.690
by getting seven to eight
hours of sleep every night

00:04:30.690 --> 00:04:32.273
in the first place.

